}_{1}{a}_{2}}{{b}_{1}{b}_{2}}=\\frac{(-2)(-2)}{(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})}=2.\n$$" 13194139535314 17592186045417 false] [17592186177303 1078 #edb/ref 17592186177308 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179808 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493906 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179809 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493925 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179809 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493948 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179813 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493935 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179814 1038 #edb/ref 17592186493907 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179939 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179939 1071 "$3-5.8=$" 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186179939 1071 "What is $3 - 5.8$?" 13194139535314 17592186045417 false] [17592186179939 1074 "Since $5.8$ is larger than $3,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem, which is to carry out the subtraction in the reverse order:\n\n$$\n5.8-3=2.8\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3-5.8=-2.8\n$$" 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186184095 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Any $1\\times4$ matrix $A$ has at most $1$ singular value.\n\n- Any $4\\times2$ matrix $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n\n- The matrix ![](images/b8/b8601b1e66ef1d302e7194f262f6a513063bba2114fb063c2fc16542d4684392.svg) has one negative singular value." 13194139535314 17592186045417 false] [17592186184095 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $1\\times4$ matrix $A$ has at most $1$ singular value.\n\nII. Any $4\\times2$ matrix $A$ has at most $2$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The matrix ![](images/b8/b8601b1e66ef1d302e7194f262f6a513063bba2114fb063c2fc16542d4684392.svg) has one negative singular value." 13194139535314 17592186045417 true] [17592186184197 103